gate:
M2 gate = M2-E4-T11 (scripts/qa/m2-gate.ps1), run only after E4-T8..T10 and E5-T13 are merged on develop and with no other worktree compiling.

AUTOMATED (agent runs `powershell -NoProfile -File scripts/qa/m2-gate.ps1 -NonInteractive`; results go to docs/design/qa/m2-gate.md with date, commit, rustc/node/pnpm, WebView2/Edge versions and session type):
1. `scripts/ci.ps1` (fmt, clippy -D warnings, test --workspace, xtask schema/gen-ts/lint-registry drift) and `scripts/ci.ps1 -Desktop` (pnpm install --frozen-lockfile, tokens:check, lint, typecheck, vitest, build).
2. `pnpm -C apps/desktop qa:check`: the automated §11 checklist (no color literals, axe 0 serious/critical, keyboard reachability with a visible focus ring, CLS < 0.01, reduced-motion <= 100 ms opacity-only, data-forge-cli on every action, error states with cause + action, remote scenario hides local_only actions), across every route in light, dark, vibrancy-off and reduced-motion.
3. `pnpm -C apps/desktop qa:shots`: full screenshot matrix (routes x light/dark x DPR 1/1.25/1.5, plus 2.0, pseudo-locale and en-US as extras) and contact sheets. These are artifacts, not a pixel gate.
4. `pnpm -C apps/desktop qa:perf`:
   - interaction < 50 ms;
   - a 500-row list scrolls at >= 55 fps with no long task > 50 ms;
   - an event storm causes <= 1 commit per frame and 0 cross-entity re-renders;
   - the slow-daemon scenario stays navigable.
5. Parity: `cargo test -p forge-cli --test cli_templates_roundtrip --test gui_parity` plus the vitest coverage check. Every argv parses with clap and maps to its method; every METHODS.cli is reached by a GUI action or listed in cli-only.yaml with a reason.
6. Cold start: build the release Forgebox.exe, then `pnpm perf:startup --runs 10` (1 discarded warm-up), daemon running and daemon stopped. The median must be < 800 ms in both cases; record p90/p95, RSS and session type (rdp/console).
7. Real-app e2e over WebView2 CDP, against a real forgeboxd in a temp portable root (fake binaries and the fake_mailpit fixture), via scripts/e2e-desktop.ps1 plus the E2/E3 live suites:
   - daemon auto-start and the status bar showing connected;
   - start/stop a service from the UI with state driven by events;
   - live PHP switch between two fake versions;
   - a quick setting;
   - a catalog install with cancel;
   - mail list;
   - terminal echo;
   - kill forgeboxd: 'reconectando' within 1 s, then a resync from seq with no duplicate Activity entries;
   - stop stuck in the cascade: GUI interactions < 50 ms;
   - second instance focuses the first.
8. Release hardening: F5, Ctrl+R, Ctrl+P, Ctrl+F, Ctrl+Shift+I, the default context menu and Ctrl+wheel zoom do nothing. The release binary has no remote-debugging argument, and src-tauri has no direct windows/windows-sys dependency (architecture guard).
9. Metrics acceptance from E5-T13 (recorded in docs/14): 1,000 req/s sustained with daemon CPU < 2 % of the machine; |p50/p90/p99 Forgebox vs oha| <= 5 %; exact request count.
10. Teardown check: no forgeboxd, Forgebox.exe or msedgewebview2 process from the temp roots remains, and nothing is written outside the temp dirs.
11. The design QA report docs/design/qa/M2-E4-report.md has every P0/P1 closed, with before/after evidence.

HUMAN (user, signed in the 'Verificação humana' table of docs/design/qa/m2-gate.md; the gate is not marked done in STATUS.md before this sign-off):
- Real Acrylic look and resize/drag smoothness at the physical console (not RDP) on Win10 19045. Confirm or adjust the Win10 default material.
- Win11, if a machine is available, otherwise explicitly deferred: Mica, snap-layout flyout, Segoe UI Variable rendering.
- Real Windows display scaling at 125/150 %, moving the window between monitors with different DPI, and window position remembered per monitor.
- Tray icons on a light and a dark taskbar; native toasts from the installed release build (AUMID).
- Global Ctrl+Alt+T; drag and drop from Explorer into Sites.
- UAC prompts started from the GUI (DNS enable, machine CA) show progress and do not look frozen.
- Cold start after a reboot (informative); a Narrator spot check.
- Subjective sign-off on the 'Apple-ish' feel and motion.

After the sign-off, the orchestrator follows ORCHESTRATION-PROMPT: create release/0.2.0, update the CHANGELOG, merge to main with tag v0.2.0, then merge back to develop. CLAUDE.md is only updated if the user approved it.

